Subject: [PATCH] Front page logo: correct bfSize to match the image it
 actually contains

236x236 at 24 bpp gives 708 bytes per row and 167088 bytes of pixel data, so with a
54-byte header the file should be 167142. bfSize claimed 167144, and
TranslateBmpToGopBlt rejects a bitmap whose header disagrees with its contents:

  BmpHeader->Size - BmpHeader->ImageOffset != DataSize

The two extra bytes are padding past the declared image, so the file is truncated to
167142 and bfSize corrected. Without this the front page logo never converts and the
title bar layout that depends on it fails.
---
 .../RawFiles/Logo                             | Bin 167144 -> 167142 bytes
 1 file changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Epsilon/BOOT.XF.3.0-00527-SM8150LZB-1/RawFiles/Logo b/Epsilon/BOOT.XF.3.0-00527-SM8150LZB-1/RawFiles/Logo
